(LST2-73 — `but if` is a generic conditional branch over ANY base action,
 not only loop expansion: over a plain `print`, and inside a handwritten
 `For each` loop. When a condition holds, the alternative runs INSTEAD of
 the base action (the plain print never prints 8).
 Also covers: LST2-77 (the default action is the base statement),
 LST2-79 (a true condition replaces the default), LST2-80 (no match means
 the default runs), LST2-84 (the alternative may be any Vox statement —
 a Set and a function call, not just a print), LST2-86 (works with both
 ranges and collections), LST2-87 (the loop variable is available in the
 conditions).
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox LST2-73.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   high
   1
   even
   3
   even
   1
   3
   6
   1
   shout 2
   3
)
To shout of a number called mark.
  print "shout {mark}".

a number called gauge is 8.
print gauge, but if gauge is greater than 5 print "high".

a list called gauges is [1, 2, 3, 4].
For each gauge2 in gauges,
  print gauge2, but if gauge2 modulo 2 is equal to 0 print "even".

a number called total is 0.
print each step from 1 to 4,
    but if the step modulo 2 is equal to 0 set total to total add step.
print total.

print each step from 1 to 3,
    but if the step is equal to 2 shout of the step.
